  "long_range_capacity": {
    "version": 1,
    "description": "Optional vocabulary for the global (k-space) operator layer; see docs/developer/execution_planner.md for workspace and capacity reporting. A capacity probe carries it as a long_range block only when its model has that layer; probes and manifests without it are unaffected.",
    "probe_fields": {
      "n_k": "positive int; half-sphere k-point count flattened over graphs. At fixed k-cut it grows linearly with cell volume (N_k ~= V*k_c^3/(12*pi^2) for orthogonal cells), so molecular systems in large vacuum boxes pay n_k proportional to box volume.",
      "table_bytes": "non-negative int; dense cos/sin table bytes = 2 * n_k * atoms * dtype itemsize (fp32: 8 * n_k * atoms; fp64: 16 * n_k * atoms). Both tables are [n_k, atoms], dominate the layer's memory, and are rebuilt every step.",
      "correction_mode": "one of correction_modes; the analytic O(N) correction terms selected by the graph pbc class.",
      "rebuild_on_cell_change": "bool; true when a cell change forces the k-grid, masks, per-k factors, and tables to rebuild. Fixed-cell steps rebuild only the tables (one K*R^T GEMM plus transcendentals); under NPT every step pays the full rebuild."
    },
    "correction_modes": {
